WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.030
When you get a bunch of big Hollywood stars
together, there's bound to be some tension.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.810
Even if their characters are getting along
on-screen, the actors behind the scenes don't

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:09.920
always see eye to eye.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.180
Here are a few actors who just couldn't stand
working together.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.720
Dustin Hoffman and Meryl Streep

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.100
Dustin Hoffman and Meryl Streep's working
relationship on the set of the Oscar-winning

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.280
film Kramer vs. Kramer played out a lot like
the divorced couple they were playing on screen.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.960
Over the years, Streep has been vocal about
the intensity that Hoffman brought to each

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.480
scene, which often startled her, and sometimes
downright scared her.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.200
Streep told CBS News just how far Hoffman
would go on set:

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:43.100
"In another scene he sapped me and when you
I see the movie I see the imprint of his hand

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.270
on the thing."

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:44.900
She added:

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.500
"I think [Hoffman is] very, very gifted, [but]
it wasn't the most fun I've ever had on film."

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:51.180
Yeah, no kidding.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.660
James Franco and Tyrese Gibson

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:59.110
Much like Meryl Streep, Tyrese Gibson wasn't
happy with the intense physicality that co-star

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:04.690
James Franco brought to the set of 2006's
Annapolis, particularly when it came to shooting

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.220
the film's big boxing match.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.720
Gibson described the experience to Elle magazine.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.780
"Whenever we'd have to get in the ring for
boxing scenes, and even during practice, the

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.580
dude was full-on hitting me."

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:19.490
Franco later apologized for his behavior,
telling GQ, "I was probably a jerk.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:23.641
I was not purposely cruel to him, but I was
probably so wrapped up in my performance that

00:01:23.641 --> 00:01:25.400
I was not as friendly as I could have been."

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.960
Charlize Theron and Tom Hardy

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:32.820
Charlize Theron and Tom Hardy had a love-hate
relationship on the set of George Miller's

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.740
2015 dystopian epic, Mad Max: Fury Road.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:42.820
Okay, make that a hate-hate relationship.

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:47.420
The Oscar-winning actress put it bluntly in
an interview with Esquire, saying that she

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.760
and Hardy "f***ing went at it" on the set.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.020
"It was the isolation, and the fact that we
were stuck in a rig for the entire shoot.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.900
We shot a war movie on a moving truck — there's
very little green screen.

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.000
It was like a family road trip that just never
went anywhere.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.060
We never got anywhere.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.080
We just drove.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.430
We drove into nothingness, and that was maddening
sometimes."

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.479
She also added that even though the actors
"drove each other crazy," they still had an

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.380
immense amount of respect for one another.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.160
Hardy even left her a semi-sentimental note
after it was done, which read, "You are an

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.440
absolute nightmare, BUT you are also f***ing
awesome.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:21.820
I'll kind of miss you.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:22.800
Love, Tommy."

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:25.120
Tom Hardy and Shia LaBeouf

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.200
Hardy's history of beefing with co-stars didn't
start with Theron.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:34.120
He also reportedly got in a fist fight with
Shia LaBeouf on the set of 2012's Lawless

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.140
— which LaBeouf apparently won.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:41.020
Hardy himself later admitted as much, although
his description of the fight sounded a little

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:42.030
tongue-in-cheek:

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.240
"He knocked me out sparko.

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.240
Out cold.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.640
He's a bad, bad boy.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.160
He is.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.720
He's quite intimidating as well.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.020
He's a scary dude...he just attacked me.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.610
He was drinking moonshine."

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:55.680
For his part, LaBeouf claimed the liquor had
nothing to do with his aggression toward Hardy,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:00.820
telling MTV that their on-set battle "wasn't
moonshine related at all" and was instead

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.520
"straight love."

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.980
"We were playing brothers.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:07.231
There was a constant finger-in-the-ear [teasing]
thing going on for a while…it was all love.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.400
I love the dude like a brother, straight up."

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.960
Jennie Garth and Shannen Doherty

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.420
These teen TV queens were on top of the world
when they shared the screen in Beverly Hills,

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:22.540
90210, but Jennie Garth and Shannen Doherty
had a very hard time getting along with each

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:23.280
other on the set.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:27.900
In her 2014 tell-all book Deep Thoughts From
a Hollywood Blonde, Garth wrote:

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.380
"I don't know why it is, but there is a universal
truth that when you put three teenage girls

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.770
together, some serious s**t is going to go
down…there were times when we loved each

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.640
other and there were times when we wanted
to claw each other's eyes out."

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.790
In 2012, Shannen Doherty revealed that whatever
rivalry had developed between the pair had

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.790
since subsided, telling Glamour:

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:52.120
"I did the new 90210 with Jennie and there
was something very different about our friendship.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.180
We were able to look at each other as grown
women and really acknowledge that we liked

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.459
who the other person was now as adults."

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:02.140
But as it turns out, you don't have to be
a teenage girl to want to smack your co-star.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.800
You can be a golden one, too.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.060
Bea Arthur and Betty White

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.900
Betty White is so likable that it's hard to
imagine anyone not wanting to become her best

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:11.400
friend.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:16.760
Unfortunately, White's upbeat personality
didn't mesh well with co-star Bea Arthur during

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:19.360
the filming of their iconic sitcom The Golden
Girls.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:23.380
White revealed during a 2013 panel discussion
with The New York Times:

00:04:23.389 --> 00:04:26.569
"We were all close, but our personalities
were all so different.

00:04:26.569 --> 00:04:30.379
[Bea] found me a pain in the neck sometimes
because [of] my positive attitude.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.919
I'm happy all the time, and that made Bea
mad sometimes."

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.780
"Woah is me.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:35.820
Woah."

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:39.300
"bad puppet."

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.580
Freddie Prinze Jr. and Kiefer Sutherland

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:47.379
Jack Bauer might have been a fan-favorite
superstar of the small screen, but Kiefer

00:04:47.379 --> 00:04:51.960
Sutherland's co-star Freddie Prinze Jr. absolutely
despised working with the actor on the set

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.840
of 24.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.210
He told ABC News:

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.920
"Kiefer was the most unprofessional dude in
the world.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:01.610
That's not me talking trash, I'd say it to
his face, I think everyone that's worked with

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.280
him has said that."

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.900
Prinze's dislike for Sutherland extended so
far that he said he even considered quitting

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:08.880
show business after working with him.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.300
Why was Prinze was so bothered by Sutherland?

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.020
For one, Prinze had to take his shoes off
to do scenes with him for the show, because

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.320
he was so much taller than Sutherland.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.580
"Just put the guy on an apple box or don't
hire me next time.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.550
You know I'm 6 feet and he's 5'4."

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:24.200
Hey, it could have been worse.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.680
After all, this is Jack Bauer we're talking
about.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.240
"I just watched my father die, and I felt
nothing."

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.219
Jeez.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:33.940
Just take off your shoes, man.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.580
Thanks for watching!

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.300
